= Sample statistics

Given:

$ n = 12 $

$ s = 4 "mm" $

The mean of the sample is

$ macron(x) = 1 / n sum_(i=1)^n x_i $

and the standard error of that mean is

$ "SE" = s / sqrt(n) $

A confidence interval follows as

$ macron(x) plus.minus t dot "SE" $
